From: sheng-development
Subject: [PATCH] Retry the SSC lookup without paying a fixed delay

The QRTR node for the SSC service is not up the instant sensorspd starts, so
debian-sheng's wait_for_qmi_service.patch wrapped the lookup in a retry loop.
That loop never terminates early:

	for (int attempt = 0; attempt < 5; attempt++) {
		sleep(1);
		for (GList *l = qrtr_bus_peek_nodes (priv->bus); l != NULL; l = l->next) {
			node = l->data;

			if (node && qrtr_node_lookup_port (node, QMI_SERVICE_SSC) >= 0) {
				found = TRUE;
				break;
			}
		}
	}

The break leaves the inner GList walk, not the attempt loop, and sleep(1) runs
before the lookup instead of after a failed one. Creating an SSC client costs a
flat 5 s whether the service is already registered or not.

iio-sensor-proxy creates one client per sensor type and waits for each in turn,
so the accelerometer is third of four to arrive and auto-rotate only works
~20 s after the service starts. The lookup it is waiting on takes 8 ms:

	03:38:50.232226  Found SSC proximity at /sys/devices/virtual/misc/fastrpc-adsp
	03:38:50.232492  [qrtr] initial lookup finished
	03:38:55.236608  QRTR node discovered for SSC service
	03:38:55.242570  Found SSC light at /sys/devices/virtual/misc/fastrpc-adsp

Check before sleeping and stop at the first hit. Modelled on-device by stubbing
sleep() out with LD_PRELOAD, all four sensors are found within 16 ms of each
other and the accelerometer reaches the bus in 0.24 s instead of 20 s.

Raise the budget to 20 attempts while here. It is only spent when the service
really is absent, and it now covers the cold-boot window that the ExecStartPre
sleep in iio-sensor-proxy's 10-sheng-sensors.conf used to hide.
--- a/src/libssc-client.c
+++ b/src/libssc-client.c
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@
  */

 #include "libssc-client-private.h"
+#include <unistd.h>
+
+#define SSC_LOOKUP_ATTEMPTS 20

 enum {
 	SIGNAL_REPORT,
@@ -361,15 +364,22 @@
 		return;
 	}

-	/* Find QRTR node for SSC service */
-	for (GList *l = qrtr_bus_peek_nodes (priv->bus); l != NULL; l = l->next) {
-		node = l->data;
-
-		if (node && qrtr_node_lookup_port (node, QMI_SERVICE_SSC) >= 0) {
-			found = TRUE;
-			break;
+	/* sensorspd takes a moment to appear on QRTR after it starts. Stop at the
+	 * first hit: iio-sensor-proxy pays this wait once per sensor type.
+	 */
+	for (guint attempt = 0; !found && attempt < SSC_LOOKUP_ATTEMPTS; attempt++) {
+		if (attempt > 0)
+			sleep (1);
+
+		for (GList *l = qrtr_bus_peek_nodes (priv->bus); l != NULL; l = l->next) {
+			node = l->data;
+
+			if (node && qrtr_node_lookup_port (node, QMI_SERVICE_SSC) >= 0) {
+				found = TRUE;
+				break;
+			}
 		}
 	}

 	if (!found) {
 		g_debug ("Service SSC not found");
